Z||000001||BlackARROW||07-06-2001||12:44 AM||||Oil Filter?  Hmm..  Are there any big differences?  A FRAM filter should work out good.<P>I just did my oil change this evening, and I chose Castrol GTX 20w50.  First time I put 20w50 - since I keep "racing" all day long with it, I opted for viscosity. I've heard somewhere it's better, since the motor tends to heat up a little bit in these conditions.<P>I think it's personnal, like tire brand preferences  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Castrol, Quaker State, Mobil 1 - whatever (just don't buy the cheap recycled ones like Nugold  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>BlackARROW<BR>'85 2m4<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||85blackgt||07-06-2001||12:55 AM||||thanks dude!<BR>20w 40 that sound like diesel? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||new fiero||07-06-2001||01:22 AM||||20W50<P>Sounds like he is running synthetic.  From what I hear it is the way to go!!<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierojunky||07-06-2001||09:16 AM||||I thought Fram was Ford?  Anyways i use AC Delco filters PF52 and Kendall Oil the Supurb100||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||07-06-2001||09:33 AM||||I use an AC PF52 filter with Valvoline 10W30.  I wouldn't use 20W40 or 20W50 unless you race or it's a very high mileage engine. ||||reg||6
Z||000006||LarryB||07-06-2001||10:28 AM||||Use the recommended 5W30 unless you want to try 10W30 in a higher-mileage engine that shows low oil pressure at idle w/5W30. Anything higher than that should be reserved as a stopgap/last resort for a very tired engine.<P>Fram is probably the best filter although AC-Delco PC-52 is fine as well. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DecadenceR||07-06-2001||11:19 AM||||Personally I use eiher Fram or PureOne filter, and 10w30 Castrol GTX.||||reg||1
